			"type": "text",
			"text": "Sinotyrannus was a theropod discovered in the Jiufotang Formation of People's Republic of China, dating back to the Early Cretaceous. Its name means 'Chinese Tyrant' as a reference to 'tyrannosaurus'. Sinotyrannus was about 9 to 10 meters long and weighed 2.5 metric tons. It is speculated that the compsognathid Huaxiagnathus might be a juvenile specimen of Sinotyrannus if this is the case, that makes Sinotyrannus a junior synonym of Huaxiagnathus."
